Path: ext-anon -CAN_ASSUME-> role-ci -GRANTS-> pol-ci-deploy -PERMITS-> s3:PutObject@res-prod-artifacts -TARGETS-> res-prod-artifacts.

Fix: the external principal reaches the target only through ext-anon -> role-ci, since ext-d-partner's role-d0000 has no path to the target. Deleting ext-anon -CAN_ASSUME-> role-ci removes all external access. Internal access is kept: svc-ci still reaches the target through its own HAS_ROLE edge to role-ci.

{"path": ["ext-anon", "role-ci", "pol-ci-deploy", "s3:PutObject@res-prod-artifacts", "res-prod-artifacts"], "fix_edge": {"from_id": "ext-anon", "type": "CAN_ASSUME", "to_id": "role-ci"}}

7.text:
Path: ext-anon -CAN_ASSUME-> role-ci -GRANTS-> pol-ci-deploy -PERMITS-> s3:PutObject@res-prod-artifacts -TARGETS-> res-prod-artifacts.

The edge to delete is ext-anon -[CAN_ASSUME]-> role-ci. It is the only external access to the target: ext-partner reaches only role-d0000, which does not lead to the bucket. Removing it also keeps svc-ci's access via HAS_ROLE to role-ci. Deleting role-ci -GRANTS-> pol-ci-deploy would remove svc-ci's internal access, so it is not suitable.

{"path": ["ext-anon", "role-ci", "pol-ci-deploy", "s3:PutObject@res-prod-artifacts", "res-prod-artifacts"], "fix_edge": {"from_id": "ext-anon", "type": "CAN_ASSUME", "to_id": "role-ci"}}

5.text:
Path: ext-contractor -> grp-ops -> role-batch -> pol-batch-secrets -> secretsmanager:GetSecretValue@res-cluster-creds -> res-cluster-creds.

Fix edge: the external principal's access runs only through ext-contractor -MEMBER_OF-> grp-ops, grp-ops -HAS_ROLE-> role-batch, and role-batch's grant. Internal access has to be kept: svc-batch has role-batch via HAS_ROLE, and u-ops-0, u-ops-1 and u-ops-2 reach it through grp-ops. Deleting ext-contractor -MEMBER_OF-> grp-ops removes only the external access and leaves every internal path intact. Deleting grp-ops -HAS_ROLE-> role-batch would cut the ops users' access, and deleting a GRANTS or PERMITS edge would cut svc-batch's access too. So the MEMBER_OF edge is the only edge that meets the requirement.

{"path": ["ext-contractor", "grp-ops", "role-batch", "pol-batch-secrets", "secretsmanager:GetSecretValue@res-cluster-creds", "res-cluster-creds"], "fix_edge": {"from_id": "ext-contractor", "type": "MEMBER_OF", "to_id": "grp-ops"}}
